{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nu=json.load(open('submissions/68dce962924a4244bd9688bff78649ed/inputs/update.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(u,indent=1)[:6000])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"rationale\": \"Review the retained logical-deadline case and consolidate it with the main and control receipts. The timeout receipt holds: the wrong-context batch did not complete before the 50-tick deadline, returned RequestTimeout at logical tick 51, and was removed by the GC path. This measures the bounded client endpoint and corrects the main account's prior limitation that the timeout was only source-supported. Separately trace observer ReadIndex admission and response routing to check whether the remote branch is follower-only; the source shows observers use the same leader queue and pending-read path, so the impact scope extends to observer-originated reads even though only follower-originated reads were measured.\",\n \"sources\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"leader-readindex-admission\",\n   \"file\": \"internal/raft/raft.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 1662,\n   \"end_line\": 1695,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"observer-readindex-forward\",\n   \"file\": \"internal/raft/raft.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 1878,\n   \"end_line\": 1884,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"follower-readindex-forward\",\n   \"file\": \"internal/raft/raft.go\",\n   \"start_line\": 1936,\n   \"end_line\": 1944,\n   \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n  }\n ],\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"ref\": \"@wrong-context-read-times-out\",\n   \"kind\": \"fact\",\n   \"statement\": \"In the logical-deadline case, after node 2 received the later context's reply and the real ready index was applied, the original read batch remained at index zero and did not complete before the 50-tick deadline. At logical tick 51 the pendingReadIndex GC returned RequestTimeout and removed the batch.\",\n   \"conditions\": \"Same three-peer in-process harness and later-first context ordering; a test-only in-memory ILogDB; node 2's request created with a 50-tick timeout; the applied ready index was supplied before the logical clock was advanced to 51; production code unchanged.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"readindex-confirm-handler\",\n    \"readindex-confirm\",\n    \"pending-read-addready\",\n    \"pending-read-applied\",\n    \"pending-read-gc\",\n    \"follower-readindexresp\",\n    \"node-readindex-admission\",\n    \"systemctx-identity\"\n   ],\n   \"executions\": {\n    \"c414588b5bc24b189d3df3217e37d7b7\": [\n     1\n    ]\n   }\n  },\n  {\n   \"ref\": \"@observer-readindex-same-path\",\n   \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n   \"statement\": \"handleLeaderReadIndex rejects a witness source but does not reject an observer source; it queues the request in the same readIndex path and broadcasts the confirmation heartbeat to voting members. An observer's local ReadIndex is forwarded by handleObserverReadIndex to handleFollowerReadIndex, and its response is routed through handleObserverReadIndexResp to handleFollowerReadIndexResp and the same pendingReadIndex consumer.\",\n   \"conditions\": \"The observer has a known leader, the leader has a committed entry in its current term, and the leader accepts the queued request. This is a source trace; observer-originated reads were not executed in the retained receipts.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"leader-readindex-admission\",\n    \"observer-readindex-forward\",\n    \"follower-readindex-forward\",\n    \"node-readindex-admission\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"interpretations\": [\n  {\n   \"investigation_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-question-0\",\n   \"experiment_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-experiment\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"readindex-confirm-handler\",\n    \"readindex-confirm\",\n    \"readindex-test-context\",\n    \"pending-read-addready\",\n    \"pending-read-applied\",\n    \"pending-read-gc\",\n    \"follower-readindexresp\",\n    \"node-process-ready\",\n    \"node-readindex-admission\",\n    \"systemctx-identity\",\n    \"leader-readindex-admission\",\n    \"observer-readindex-forward\",\n    \"follower-readindex-forward\"\n   ],\n   \"executions\": {\n    \"c2848ac1c82f442ba305267049bbb53b\": [\n     2,\n     3,\n     4\n    ],\n    \"55e578441ac24bde9e837485d2c078a6\": [\n     1,\n     2\n    ],\n    \"c414588b5bc24b189d3df3217e37d7b7\": [\n     1\n    ]\n   },\n   \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n   \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n   \"rationale\": \"The current conclusion remains a bounded liveness and client-contract defect for follower-originated ReadIndex requests when a later queued context is confirmed first. The main receipt admits node 2's context {101,1002} at event 0 and node 3's context {202,2003} at event 1; event 2 replies to node 2 with node 3's context and log index 4; event 3 leaves node 2's original batch at index zero after the real ready index 4 was applied; event 4 shows the later context-101 confirmation produces no context-correct reply and no completion. The source cause remains the remote reply construction in handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation using the confirming heartbeat's Hint/HintHigh instead of the queued request's s.ctx, while confirm deletes the earlier queue entry and pendingReadIndex.addReady requires an exact SystemCtx key. The sequential control confirms the same consumer path with node 2's admitted context first: its reply carries that context and completion is 1 with batch index 4. The logical-deadline case keeps the later-first ordering: its event 1 records original_batch_index zero, no completion before the 50-tick deadline, RequestTimeout at advanced tick 51, and the stale batch absent after GC. Together these distinguish a context-association defect from a general consumer or harness failure and measure the bounded client endpoint. The main reply's log index is a later committed index, so no stale-read value or safety violation is established. The request remains uncompleted after a valid applied index until the measured logical timeout. Source admission also shows observers are not excluded from the leader's ReadIndex queue and use the same observer response path; the impact scope therefore includes observer-originated reads, although the retained receipts measured only follower-originated reads.\",\n   \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n     \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\",\n     \"revision\": 1,\n     \"assertion\": \"The confirming\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
