{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nu=json.load(open('submissions/68dce962924a4244bd9688bff78649ed/inputs/update.json'))\nfor k in u['interpretations'][0]['knowledge']:\n    print(json.dumps(k,indent=1))\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\",\n \"revision\": 1,\n \"assertion\": \"The confirming context returns earlier queued requests while preserving each request's own SystemCtx.\"\n}\n{\n \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-1\",\n \"revision\": 1,\n \"assertion\": \"Remote replies are tagged with the confirming heartbeat context instead of the queued request's context.\"\n}\n{\n \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-2\",\n \"revision\": 1,\n \"assertion\": \"A response with a nonmatching SystemCtx leaves the original pending batch at index zero and cannot complete it.\"\n}\n{\n \"entry_id\": \"083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0\",\n \"revision\": 1,\n \"assertion\": \"The exercised later-confirmation ordering produced a mismatched reply context and left the earlier read batch unready after the ready index was applied.\"\n}\n{\n \"entry_id\": \"1457862374ac4b5bbba3c0e3588dbb50-knowledge-0\",\n \"revision\": 1,\n \"assertion\": \"The sequential-confirmation control completed when the admitted context was confirmed first.\"\n}\n{\n \"entry_id\": \"@wrong-context-read-times-out\",\n \"revision\": 1,\n \"assertion\": \"The logical-deadline case returned RequestTimeout at tick 51 and removed the stale batch.\"\n}\n{\n \"entry_id\": \"@observer-readindex-same-path\",\n \"revision\": 1,\n \"assertion\": \"Observer-originated ReadIndex requests enter the same leader queue and pending-read response path.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Interpret the retained follower snapshot-delivery receipt and fold it into the snapshot-restore account. The receipt's four comparisons all hold with matched admissions: the stale snapshot at index 3 exposed nothing and left the committed index at 4, and the newer snapshot at index 10 was exposed at index 10 and advanced the committed index to 10. That converts the stale-index guard and the committed-position advance from source-only into measured follower behavior. The membership half of the question stays source-only because both delivered snapshots carried the existing {1,2,3} membership, so the execution cannot distinguish rebuilding the role maps from merging them. The interpretation is updated with the experiment and receipt and with limitations that state that split.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n  {\n   \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@snapshot-stale-newer-measured\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fact\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"In the retained follower snapshot-delivery execution, node 2 had committed index 4 when an InstallSnapshot at index 3 arrived; the follower exposed no snapshot and its committed index stayed 4. A following InstallSnapshot at index 10 was exposed at index 10 and advanced the follower's committed index to 10.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Three real in-process Raft Peer handlers with bootstrap membership {1,2,3} and node 1 as leader with a committed current-term no-op at index 4; node 2 received InstallSnapshot messages with index 3 term 1 and index 10 term 2, each carrying the current {1,2,3} membership, through its real handler; one test-only in-memory ILogDB per node; the follower's committed index was sampled from the update state reported by each pump; production code unchanged.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"raft-restore-guard\\\", \\\"raft-log-restore\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"44629fa87bbb418b99ac46fff6cb228d\\\": [1, 3]}\n  }\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n  {\n   \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"92d09ed3d0304cadab7dd6187761d953-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\": \\\"00797d817371473babcaf5b1b7b0a7bf-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n    \\\"raft-restore-guard\\\",\\\"raft-restore-remotes\\\",\\\"raft-log-restore\\\",\\\"node-restore-remotes\\\",\n    \\\"node-push-snapshot\\\",\\\"rsm-recover-restores-remotes\\\",\\\"election-apply-gate\\\",\\\"applied-vs-committed-check\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"44629fa87bbb418b99ac46fff6cb228d\\\": [1, 3]},\n   \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"explained\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\": \\\"refuted\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The suspicion remains refuted for the captured paths, and the follower-side delivery effect is now measured rather than inferred. In the retained execution, node 2 had committed index 4 when an InstallSnapshot at index 3 arrived through its real handler: the follower exposed no snapshot and its committed index remained 4, so event 1 satisfies both the snapshot_present false and commit_after 4 comparisons and matches raft.restore's guard rejecting a snapshot whose index does not exceed the committed index. A following InstallSnapshot at index 10 was exposed at index 10 and the follower's committed index advanced to 10, so event 3 satisfies the snapshot_index 10 and commit_after 10 comparisons and matches the log restore setting the committed and processed positions to the snapshot index. The membership half of the question remains source-supported: restoreRemotes rebuilds the remotes, observers and witnesses maps from the snapshot membership with fresh allocations rather than merging, so a node absent from the snapshot is dropped rather than retained in quorum, and a leader that the snapshot removes steps down. The running-follower path reaches that replacement through the state machine's Recover task after the node applies the snapshot; during that interval the raft committed index already equals the snapshot index while the applied index lags, and handleNodeElection refuses to campaign while the committed index exceeds the applied index, so the interim membership cannot be used to start an election. raft.restore also refuses to convert the local node into an observer or witness. The measured snapshots carried the existing membership, so they show the log and commit effects of a stale and a newer installation but cannot separate a role-map rebuild from a role-map merge.\\\",\n   \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n    {\\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"92d09ed3d0304cadab7dd6187761d953-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\": 1,\\\"assertion\\\": \\\"restoreRemotes rebuilds the raft role maps from the snapshot membership, and the live path reaches it through the state machine's Recover task, so an absent node is dropped rather than merged.\\\"},\n    {\\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"@snapshot-stale-newer-measured\\\",\\\"revision\\\": 1,\\\"assertion\\\": \\\"The measured follower rejected the stale snapshot at index 3 and advanced its committed index to 10 on the newer snapshot.\\\"}\n   ],\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n    \\\"restore writes the log positions before restoreRemotes replaces the role maps, so the two are not atomic with respect to each other; the refutation relies on the election gate closing the resulting window for a non-leader.\\\",\n    \\\"A leader that receives a snapshot-derived membership steps down only when the snapshot no longer contains it; the captured paths do not exercise a leader that is asked to install a snapshot while remaining a member.\\\",\n    \\\"The role-map replacement happens in the state machine's Recover task, so its promptness depends on that task being run by the surrounding node.\\\",\n    \\\"The measured snapshots carried the current {1,2,3} membership, so the receipt's exposure and commit observations would look the same whether the role maps were rebuilt or reused; the rebuild-versus-merge claim still rests on the source.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\": [\n    \\\"Snapshot delivery is measured for one follower receiving a stale and then a newer snapshot whose membership equals its existing membership; role-map replacement, the Recover task and restart recovery remain source-only.\\\",\n    \\\"The snapshots were passed to the follower's real handler as InstallSnapshot messages, so no transport, snapshot streaming or on-disk persistence path is exercised.\\\",\n    \\\"Snapshot corruption, a storage layer that returns a snapshot inconsistent with its recorded membership, and operator-supplied snapshots are excluded.\\\",\n    \\\"The account covers the membership maps and the election gate; it does not re-derive log-matching safety for the appended entries that follow a restore.\\\",\n    \\\"Only the single-node view is traced; how peers react to a member that restored a different snapshot is not examined.\\\"\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(u, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\npython3 -c \\\"import json;json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run/draft/update.json'));print('json ok')\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
